{"id":"mahabharata-12-348","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":348,"title":"अष्टचत्वारिंशदधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 348 · The naga weighs the visit","summary":{"en":"The naga asks his wife whether the guest is a mere man or a god, and she tells of the brahmin who has come. He says that he does not know whom she sees, but that he will go where the brahmin stays and will not let him go away unsatisfied.","kn":"ಬಂದವನು ಕೇವಲ ಮನುಷ್ಯನೋ ದೇವನೋ ಎಂದು ನಾಗ ಪತ್ನಿಯನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅವಳು ಬಂದ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಅವಳು ಯಾರನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾಳೋ ತಿಳಿಯದು, ಆದರೆ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ಇರುವಲ್ಲಿಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ಅತೃಪ್ತನಾಗಿ ಕಳುಹಿಸುವುದಿಲ್ಲವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"नाग पत्नी से पूछता है कि अतिथि केवल मनुष्य है या देवता, और वह आए ब्राह्मण की बात कहती है। नाग कहता है कि वह नहीं जानता वह किसे देख रही है, पर जहाँ ब्राह्मण ठहरा है वहाँ जाएगा और उसे असन्तुष्ट नहीं लौटने देगा।","te":"వచ్చినవాడు కేవలం మనిషా లేక దేవుడా అని నాగుడు భార్యను అడుగుతాడు, ఆమె వచ్చిన బ్రాహ్మణుని గురించి చెబుతుంది. ఆమె ఎవరిని చూస్తోందో తనకు తెలియదని, కానీ బ్రాహ్మణుడు ఉన్న చోటికి వెళ్లి అతన్ని అసంతృప్తిగా పంపనని అంటాడు.","ta":"வந்தவர் வெறும் மனிதரா தெய்வமா என்று நாகன் மனைவியைக் கேட்க, அவள் வந்த அந்தணனைப் பற்றிக் கூறுகிறாள். அவள் யாரைக் காண்கிறாள் என்று தனக்குத் தெரியாது, ஆனால் அந்தணன் தங்கிய இடம் செல்வேன், அவனை நிறைவின்றி அனுப்ப மாட்டேன் என்கிறான்.","ml":"അതിഥി സാധാരണ മനുഷ്യനോ ദേവനോ എന്ന് നാഗം പത്നിയോട് ചോദിക്കുന്നു; ബ്രാഹ്മണൻ വന്നുവെന്ന് അവർ പറയുന്നു. അവൾ കാണുന്നത് ആരെന്ന് തനിക്കറിയില്ലെന്നും, എന്നാൽ ബ്രാഹ്മണൻ താമസിക്കുന്നിടത്തേക്ക് താൻ പോകുമെന്നും, അദ്ദേഹത്തെ തൃപ്തിപ്പെടുത്താതെ പോകാൻ അനുവദിക്കില്ലെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.348; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"नाग उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The naga said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथ ब्राह्मणरूपेण कं तं समनुपश्यसि ।\nमानुषं केवलं विप्रं देवं वाथ शुचिस्मिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whom do you see in that brahmin form, bright-smiling one: a mere human brahmin, or a god?"}},{"n":2,"text":"को हि मां मानुषः शक्तो द्रष्टुकामो यशस्विनि ।\nसंदर्शनरुचिर्वाक्यमाज्ञापूर्वं वदिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Glorious lady, what human could want to see me? One fond of seeing me would speak words in the form of a request, not an order."}},{"n":3,"text":"सुरासुरगणानां च देवर्षीणां च भामिनि ।\nननु नागा महावीर्याः सौरसेयास्तरस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely, fair one, the nagas, sons of Surasa, are greatly mighty and swift, even among the hosts of gods and asuras and divine sages."}},{"n":4,"text":"वन्दनीयाश्च वरदा वयमप्यनुयायिनः ।\nमनुष्याणां विशेषेण धनाध्यक्षा इति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We are worthy of homage, givers of boons, and followed by others; especially among humans we are said, in tradition, to be stewards of wealth."}},{"text":"नागभार्योवाच","meaning":{"en":"The naga's wife said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"आर्जवेनाभिजानामि नासौ देवोऽनिलाशन ।\nएकं त्वस्य विजानामि भक्तिमानतिरोषणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By my simple judgment, I know he is no god, wind-eater. I know one thing of him: he is devoted and extremely irritable."}},{"n":6,"text":"स हि कार्यान्तराकाङ्क्षी जलेप्सुः स्तोकको यथा ।\nवर्षं वर्षप्रियः पक्षी दर्शनं तव काङ्क्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He wants some other business with you, like a thirsty stoka bird, a lover of rain, longing for rain; he longs to see you."}},{"n":7,"text":"न हि त्वा दैवतं किंचिद्विविग्नं प्रतिपालयेत् ।\nतुल्ये ह्यभिजने जातो न कश्चित्पर्युपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"No god would wait for you in distress; those born of the same rank do not attend each other."}},{"n":8,"text":"तद्रोषं सहजं त्यक्त्वा त्वमेनं द्रष्टुमर्हसि ।\nआशाछेदेन तस्याद्य नात्मानं दग्धुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"So put aside your inborn anger and see him. You should not burn yourself by cutting off his hope today."}},{"n":9,"text":"आशया त्वभिपन्नानामकृत्वाश्रुप्रमार्जनम् ।\nराजा वा राजपुत्रो वा भ्रूणहत्यैव युज्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king or a king's son who does not wipe the tears of those who come in hope is guilty as of killing an embryo."}},{"n":10,"text":"मौनाज्ज्ञानफलावाप्तिर्दानेन च यशो महत् ।\nवाग्मित्वं सत्यवाक्येन परत्र च महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By silence one gains the fruit of knowledge; by giving, great fame; by truthful speech, eloquence; and one is honored in the next world."}},{"n":11,"text":"भूमिप्रदानेन गतिं लभत्याश्रमसंमिताम् ।\nनष्टस्यार्थस्य संप्राप्तिं कृत्वा फलमुपाश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the gift of land one gains a destination equal to the stages of life; having recovered lost property for someone, one reaps its fruit."}},{"n":12,"text":"अभिप्रेतामसंक्लिष्टां कृत्वाकामवतीं क्रियाम् ।\nन याति निरयं कश्चिदिति धर्मविदो विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who know dharma say that no one goes to hell who has done an act that was desired and untroubled, and carried out as wished."}},{"text":"नाग उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The naga said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"अभिमानेन मानो मे जातिदोषेण वै महान् ।\nरोषः संकल्पजः साध्वि दग्धो वाचाग्निना त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"My pride, great because of my birth's fault, and my anger, born of intention, have been burned, good lady, by the fire of your words."}},{"n":14,"text":"न च रोषादहं साध्वि पश्येयमधिकं तमः ।\nयस्य वक्तव्यतां यान्ति विशेषेण भुजंगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I would not see any deeper darkness than anger, in which especially nagas come to be spoken of."}},{"n":15,"text":"दोषस्य हि वशं गत्वा दशग्रीवः प्रतापवान् ।\nतथा शक्रप्रतिस्पर्धी हतो रामेण संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the grip of this fault the mighty ten-necked Ravana, rival of Shakra, was killed by Rama in battle."}},{"n":16,"text":"अन्तःपुरगतं वत्सं श्रुत्वा रामेण निर्हृतम् ।\nधर्षणाद्रोषसंविग्नाः कार्तवीर्यसुता हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they heard that the calf had been taken from the women's quarters by Rama, the sons of Kartavirya, troubled with anger at the insult, were killed."}},{"n":17,"text":"जामदग्न्येन रामेण सहस्रनयनोपमः ।\nसंयुगे निहतो रोषात्कार्तवीर्यो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And mighty Kartavirya, like the thousand-eyed Indra, was killed in battle in anger by Rama, son of Jamadagni."}},{"n":18,"text":"तदेष तपसां शत्रुः श्रेयसश्च निपातनः ।\nनिगृहीतो मया रोषः श्रुत्वैव वचनं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So this anger, enemy of austerity and destroyer of the good, has been restrained by me as soon as I heard your words."}},{"n":19,"text":"आत्मानं च विशेषेण प्रशंसाम्यनपायिनि ।\nयस्य मे त्वं विशालाक्षि भार्या सर्वगुणान्विता ॥","meaning":{"en":"I especially praise myself, faultless one, since you, wide-eyed, endowed with every virtue, are my wife."}},{"n":20,"text":"एष तत्रैव गच्छामि यत्र तिष्ठत्यसौ द्विजः ।\nसर्वथा चोक्तवान्वाक्यं नाकृतार्थः प्रयास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will go right where that brahmin stays. He said it in every way: he will not leave with his purpose unfulfilled."}}]}]}